TITLE:: SampleEditorHost
summary:: what a SampleEditor knows of the world: where the preview plays, and who hears of the files it writes
categories:: Libraries>SampleEditor
related:: Classes/SampleEditor, Classes/SampleEditorDirtHost, Classes/SampleEdit

DESCRIPTION::
The editor, its model and its slicer ask their host where the preview plays,
which Buffer to play from and what a sample library calls a file, and they tell
it about every file they write. This class is the editor on its own: the
preview goes to the server's hardware outputs (the menu beside play lists them
in pairs), a file is read into a Buffer of the editor's own and freed with the
window, and written files are only written. There is no tag store, so a bpm,
key or tags set in the window last as long as the window.

code::
SampleEditor("~/x.wav", SampleEditorHost(s));
SampleEditor.defaultHost = SampleEditorHost(s);     // for every editor from now on
::

link::Classes/SampleEditorDirtHost:: is the host inside a SuperDirt. Anything
else can be a host by answering the messages below: they are the whole of what
the editor asks.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: server
nil for code::Server.default::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: server
The Server the preview plays on.

METHOD:: numChannels
How many channels the preview writes: 2.

METHOD:: outputNames
The menu beside play, one String per output: code::"out 0-1"::, code::"out 2-3":: ...

METHOD:: outputLabel
METHOD:: outputHint
The menu's label and hint.

METHOD:: playTarget
Where the preview synth goes for an output.
ARGUMENT:: i
the output's index.
RETURNS:: code::(target:, bus:, addAction:)::.

METHOD:: wake
Called just before the preview starts on an output, at the server's latency.
ARGUMENT:: i
the output's index.

METHOD:: bufferFor
A Buffer already holding the file, or nil for the editor to read one. Called
inside a Routine: it may sync.
ARGUMENT:: path
the file.

METHOD:: sampleAt
The file as a library knows it.
ARGUMENT:: path
the file.
RETURNS:: code::[name, index]::, or nil.

METHOD:: pathOf
The file a library holds as name:index, or nil.
ARGUMENT:: name
the bank.
ARGUMENT:: index
the sample in it.

METHOD:: bankSize
How many samples a bank holds now (the to bank... window's preview).
ARGUMENT:: name
the bank.

METHOD:: fileChanged
A file was written over: a save or a revert.
ARGUMENT:: path
the file.

METHOD:: fileAdded
A file was written into the folder of a bank (save as).
ARGUMENT:: path
the new file.
ARGUMENT:: bank
the bank's name.

METHOD:: folderWritten
New files in a bank's folder: to bank... and export slices....
ARGUMENT:: folder
the folder.
ARGUMENT:: paths
the files written.
RETURNS:: the names of the banks loaded, or nil.

METHOD:: store
Where a file's bpm, key and tags are kept, or nil. A store answers
SuperDirtGUI's code::SDGSampleTags:: messages: code::infoOf::,
code::setBpm::, code::setKey::, code::setTags::, code::addTag::,
code::analyse::, code::enqueue::, and sends code::\tags:: when they change.

METHOD:: soundExtensions
The kinds of file the library reads: wav and aiff, as SuperDirt. A file of
another kind is written as WAV for a bank.

METHOD:: samplesFolder
Where banks go by default: Dirt-Samples when SuperDirt is installed
(link::Classes/SampleCutter#*samplesFolder::), else nil.
